{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this stay. You were just admitted for nausea and vomiting again, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I just can’t keep anything down. I feel so sick every time I try to eat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your blood pressure was very high when you came in—194 over 94. That’s concerning. Did you notice any headaches or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no chest pain or headaches. Just the nausea and throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good. We’re giving you IV fluids to help with dehydration. Your lab work showed a high lactate level earlier—4.6—which suggests your body was under stress from not having enough fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lactate? Is that like acidosis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s called lactic acidosis. But after three liters of IV fluids, your lactate dropped to 1.0, which is normal. So that’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s good. But why does this keep happening? I was just here two days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we’re trying to understand. You have gastroparesis, which means your stomach empties slowly. But we’ve also noticed that sometimes vomiting happens right after you drink or eat, even if it’s small amounts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can’t help it. I just feel so full and sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But one of the nurses saw you induce vomiting after drinking water. Is that something you do when you feel anxious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… I don’t know. Maybe. It just feels like the only way to stop the nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I want you to know we’re not judging you. But induced vomiting can make everything worse—dehydration, acidosis, even high blood pressure. It’s a cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So you think it’s in my head?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not exactly. Your gastroparesis is real. But the way you respond—vomiting right after intake—suggests a behavioral pattern, possibly linked to anxiety. That’s why psychiatry has been consulted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve missed some appointments. I know I should go, but I get too anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-05-08 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. The important thing is recognizing it now. We can help you set up a new appointment before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, but I didn’t vomit last night. I tried sipping water slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. Your blood pressure is better too—142 over 88 this morning. We’ve switched you from IV labetalol to oral meds: lisinopril and amlodipine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on lisinopril before. Why the new one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because your blood pressure was so high, we needed an extra medication. Amlodipine helps relax your blood vessels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my insulin? My sugars have been high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you glargine at night and lispro with meals. Since you’re not eating much, we’re using a sliding scale to adjust doses safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had the gastric pacer for a reason. Why isn’t it helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pacer helps some, but it can’t override the effects of frequent vomiting or anxiety. We also discussed a J-tube, but you decided against it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want surgery. I just want to stop feeling like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-05-09 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And that’s possible. But it will take work—both medically and with mental health support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray yesterday was clear—no pneumonia or aspiration. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was worried about that. I’ve thrown up so much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. But your lungs look good. The main issue remains the cycle of vomiting, dehydration, and high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been thinking. Maybe the vomiting does help me feel temporary relief, but then I feel worse after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a really important insight. It’s like a coping mechanism, but it’s harming your body in the long run."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what can I do instead?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-05-10 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with psychiatry to find strategies—maybe different medications or therapy techniques to manage the urge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve gone two full days without vomiting. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel nauseous, but I’ve been using the Zofran and trying deep breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. And your labs are stable—no acidosis, hemoglobin is holding, and your electrolytes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge tomorrow, yes. But we want to make sure you’re safe with follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll go to psychiatry this time. I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll schedule it before you leave. And we’re giving you Zofran for breakthrough nausea, plus your regular Reglan and Nexium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure pills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-05-11 08:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take lisinopril 10 mg three times a day and amlodipine twice daily. We lowered the lisinopril dose to avoid low BP now that you’re hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-05-12 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge. You’ve been off IV fluids for 24 hours, eating small meals, and no vomiting. How do you feel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-05-12 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired, but better. I’m scared it’ll come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-05-12 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. But you’ve made real progress by acknowledging the role of anxiety. That’s the first step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-05-12 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep working on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-05-12 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll support you. Discharge is set for tomorrow morning. Rest up, and the nurse will review your meds and instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-05-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Remember: take your meds, eat small meals, and call if nausea returns. Most importantly—keep your psychiatry appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2199-05-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really want to get better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2199-05-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And we believe you can. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-05-08 14:09:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-05-13 12:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and a history of anxiety was readmitted two days after discharge for recurrent nausea and vomiting. She presented with hypertensive crisis (BP 194/94) and lactic acidosis due to volume depletion, both of which improved with IV fluids and antihypertensive therapy. Throughout the hospitalization, she was observed inducing vomiting, leading to the recognition that her symptoms were primarily driven by a psychiatric condition. After discussions with GI and psychiatry, she acknowledged the psychological basis of her vomiting and committed to outpatient follow-up. Her diet was advanced, medications were optimized, and she was discharged home in stable condition with a plan for ongoing mental health support.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastrointestinal malfunction arising from mental factors",
      "Acidosis",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Volume depletion, unspecified",
      "Personal history of infections of the central nervous system"
    ]
  }
}
